<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Capitulation of Wittenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1547</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-war">Schmalkaldic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Capitulation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a> of 19 May 1547 was the settlement imposed by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> on the captive Elector John Frederick I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-muhlberg">Battle of Mühlberg</a>. John Frederick surrendered the electoral title and much of his territory, including Wittenberg, to his Albertine cousin Maurice, keeping only lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> for his sons. The Ernestine line never regained the electorate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/capitulation-of-wittenberg.jpg" alt="Capitulation of Wittenberg" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Saxony_after_the_Capitulation_of_Wittenberg_(1547)_-_NL.png: Sir Iain derivative work: Furfur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saxony_after_the_Capitulation_of_Wittenberg_(1547)_-_DE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
